# =============================================================================
# oc-ask ignore rules — added 2026-08-28.
#
# This repo had no .gitignore at all, and both paths below are auto-generated
# artifacts with timestamped or append-only names, i.e. they grow without bound.
# They were committed in 7ec529b while still trivial (~100 KB) precisely because
# nothing excluded them.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE RULES ARE WORKING: .gitignore NEVER applies to a
# file already in the index. The 21 files under logs/ and .ai/telemetry/ that
# 7ec529b tracked stay tracked, and keep getting committed, until someone runs
# `git rm --cached` on them. That asymmetry is how the sibling repo accumulated
# 4.70 GB behind ignore rules that were already correct — see
# opencode_memory/2026-08-28_repo_cleanup_fork_and_47gb_rewrite.md §5.
# These rules therefore only stop NEW files here.
# =============================================================================

# sqlmesh run logs — timestamped names, 288 bytes each, two boilerplate lines
logs/

# append-only validator telemetry
.ai/telemetry/
